{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-20201","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21263","text":"PULSE v0.2 — Behavioral Loop Types"}]},{"id":"blk-20202","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21264","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-21265","text":" Design proposal (2026-05-27) — for review before implementation."}]},{"id":"blk-20203","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21266","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal:"},{"id":"spn-21267","text":" Promote PULSE from a *structural schema* (named phases + named tokens) to a *typed protocol* (session-typed phases + linear tokens + projected choreography). Bring formal-spec quality to the level of behavioral type systems without losing the implementation maturity of v0.1.1."}]},{"id":"blk-20204","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21268","text":"Why"}]},{"id":"blk-20205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21269","text":"PULSE v0.1.1 declares 5 phase kinds, 6 cross-loop tokens, and 7 invariants. The schema validates *names and shapes* but cannot answer:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20207","spans":[{"id":"spn-21270","text":"Question v0.1.1 cannot answer"}]},{"id":"blk-20208","spans":[{"id":"spn-21271","text":"What's needed"}]}],"id":"blk-20206","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20209","spans":[{"id":"spn-21272","text":"Is this manifest deadlock-free?"}]},{"id":"blk-20210","spans":[{"id":"spn-21273","text":"Session-typed phase graph"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20211","spans":[{"id":"spn-21274","text":"Will every emitted "},{"id":"spn-21275","marks":["code"],"text":"SurpriseSignal"},{"id":"spn-21276","text":" be consumed?"}]},{"id":"blk-20212","spans":[{"id":"spn-21277","text":"Linear token typing"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20213","spans":[{"id":"spn-21278","text":"Is "},{"id":"spn-21279","marks":["code"],"text":"loop@v2"},{"id":"spn-21280","text":" a safe drop-in replacement for "},{"id":"spn-21281","marks":["code"],"text":"loop@v1"},{"id":"spn-21282","text":"?"}]},{"id":"blk-20214","spans":[{"id":"spn-21283","text":"Behavioral subtyping"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20215","spans":[{"id":"spn-21284","text":"If loop A sends X, will loop B receive a compatible X?"}]},{"id":"blk-20216","spans":[{"id":"spn-21285","text":"Multiparty choreography + projection"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20217","spans":[{"id":"spn-21286","text":"Does this phase's declared effect match its runtime behavior?"}]},{"id":"blk-20218","spans":[{"id":"spn-21287","text":"Effect rows + runtime fidelity check"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20219","spans":[{"id":"spn-21288","text":"Are the declared invariants actually true of this manifest?"}]},{"id":"blk-20220","spans":[{"id":"spn-21289","text":"Refinement-type checker"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20221","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21290","text":"Behavioral type systems (session types, multiparty session types, behavioral contracts) answer exactly these questions — but as preprints, not as running software. PULSE v0.2 ports the answers into a JSON-Schema-grounded substrate that already has 5 reference manifests and a conformance suite."}]},{"id":"blk-20222","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21291","text":"What it buys (scorecard delta)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20224","spans":[{"id":"spn-21292","text":"Axis"}]},{"id":"blk-20225","spans":[{"id":"spn-21293","text":"v0.1.1"}]},{"id":"blk-20226","spans":[{"id":"spn-21294","text":"v0.2"}]},{"id":"blk-20227","spans":[{"id":"spn-21295","text":"Why"}]}],"id":"blk-20223","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20228","spans":[{"id":"spn-21296","text":"Formality"}]},{"id":"blk-20229","spans":[{"id":"spn-21297","text":"8"}]},{"id":"blk-20230","spans":[{"id":"spn-21298","marks":["bold"],"text":"10"}]},{"id":"blk-20231","spans":[{"id":"spn-21299","text":"Session-type-grade; refinement types on cadence/invariants; effect rows on phases"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20232","spans":[{"id":"spn-21300","text":"Compositionality"}]},{"id":"blk-20233","spans":[{"id":"spn-21301","text":"7"}]},{"id":"blk-20234","spans":[{"id":"spn-21302","marks":["bold"],"text":"10"}]},{"id":"blk-20235","spans":[{"id":"spn-21303","text":"Choreography + projection; linear tokens; behavioral subtyping"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20236","spans":[{"id":"spn-21304","text":"Substrate independence"}]},{"id":"blk-20237","spans":[{"id":"spn-21305","text":"9"}]},{"id":"blk-20238","spans":[{"id":"spn-21306","marks":["bold"],"text":"10"}]},{"id":"blk-20239","spans":[{"id":"spn-21307","text":"Typed protocol portable to any language with a type system"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20240","spans":[{"id":"spn-21308","text":"Closure"}]},{"id":"blk-20241","spans":[{"id":"spn-21309","text":"7"}]},{"id":"blk-20242","spans":[{"id":"spn-21310","marks":["bold"],"text":"9"}]},{"id":"blk-20243","spans":[{"id":"spn-21311","text":"Liveness + fidelity machine-checked; loses 1 for new verifier dependency"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20244","spans":[{"id":"spn-21312","marks":["bold"],"text":"Total / 40"}]},{"id":"blk-20245","spans":[{"id":"spn-21313","marks":["bold"],"text":"31"}]},{"id":"blk-20246","spans":[{"id":"spn-21314","marks":["bold"],"text":"39"}]},{"id":"blk-20247","spans":[{"id":"spn-21315","text":""}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20248","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21316","text":"For external context see "},{"id":"spn-21317","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/V0.2-BEHAVIORAL-TYPES-RATIONALE.md"},{"id":"spn-21318","text":" (planned) which compares this against Agent Behavioral Contracts (preprint), AgentRFC, and the CCS/CSP ceiling."}]},{"id":"blk-20249","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21319","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-20250","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21320","text":"The six additions"}]},{"id":"blk-20251","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21321","text":"1. Typed token registry"}]},{"id":"blk-20252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21322","marks":["bold"],"text":"File:"},{"id":"spn-21323","text":" "},{"id":"spn-21324","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas/pulse-tokens.v0.2.json"},{"id":"spn-21325","text":" (new)"}]},{"id":"blk-20253","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21326","text":"Each canonical token gets a payload schema, a linearity annotation, a variance annotation, and a TTL."}]},{"id":"blk-20254","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"tokens\": {\n    \"TopologyContext\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/topology_context.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 60000,\n      \"description\": \"Emitted by retrieve, consumed by route. Loss would blind routing — must be consumed.\"\n    },\n    \"DeliberationRequest\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/deliberation_request.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 300000,\n      \"description\": \"Triggers an inner deliberation loop. Loss would silently skip κ-resolution.\"\n    },\n    \"DeliberationResult\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/deliberation_result.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 300000\n    },\n    \"OutcomeSignal\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/outcome_signal.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 3600000,\n      \"description\": \"Audit primitive. Every action result must produce one — drop = audit failure.\"\n    },\n    \"ReputationUpdate\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/reputation_update.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"affine\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 86400000,\n      \"description\": \"Long-window aggregation; tolerates loss (drop down from linear because the next update overrides anyway).\"\n    },\n    \"ConsolidationEvent\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/consolidation_event.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"affine\",\n      \"variance\": \"covariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 3600000,\n      \"description\": \"Housekeeping signal; consolidate is idempotent.\"\n    },\n    \"SurpriseSignal\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/surprise_signal.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 60000,\n      \"description\": \"OS-011 forward-model-prediction-error. Must be consumed.\"\n    },\n    \"SessionFidelityViolation\": {\n      \"payload_schema\": \"schemas/tokens/session_fidelity_violation.v0.2.json\",\n      \"linearity\": \"linear\",\n      \"variance\": \"invariant\",\n      \"ttl_ms\": 86400000,\n      \"description\": \"Runtime-observed protocol violation. Must be reported, never silently dropped.\"\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-20255","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21327","marks":["bold"],"text":"Default for new canonical tokens: `linear`."},{"id":"spn-21328","text":" Authors must explicitly opt down to "},{"id":"spn-21329","marks":["code"],"text":"affine"},{"id":"spn-21330","text":" only when the token is observational, idempotent, or inherently lossy-tolerant (next emission overrides previous). This default flows from OS-010's \"every consequential signal must be audited\" thesis — silent loss is an audit failure; duplication is detected via idempotency keys at the substrate boundary."}]},{"id":"blk-20256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21331","marks":["bold"],"text":"Linearity values:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20258","spans":[{"id":"spn-21332","text":"Value"}]},{"id":"blk-20259","spans":[{"id":"spn-21333","text":"Meaning"}]},{"id":"blk-20260","spans":[{"id":"spn-21334","text":"Checker enforces"}]}],"id":"blk-20257","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20261","spans":[{"id":"spn-21335","marks":["code"],"text":"linear"}]},{"id":"blk-20262","spans":[{"id":"spn-21336","text":"Exactly-once consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-20263","spans":[{"id":"spn-21337","text":"Emit ⇒ exactly one consumer; consumer is unique"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20264","spans":[{"id":"spn-21338","marks":["code"],"text":"affine"}]},{"id":"blk-20265","spans":[{"id":"spn-21339","text":"At-most-once consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-20266","spans":[{"id":"spn-21340","text":"Emit ⇒ at most one consumer (may drop)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20267","spans":[{"id":"spn-21341","marks":["code"],"text":"relevant"}]},{"id":"blk-20268","spans":[{"id":"spn-21342","text":"At-least-once consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-20269","spans":[{"id":"spn-21343","text":"Emit ⇒ at least one consumer (may duplicate)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20270","spans":[{"id":"spn-21344","marks":["code"],"text":"unrestricted"}]},{"id":"blk-20271","spans":[{"id":"spn-21345","text":"Any consumption"}]},{"id":"blk-20272","spans":[{"id":"spn-21346","text":"No constraint"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21347","marks":["bold"],"text":"Variance values:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20275","spans":[{"id":"spn-21348","text":"Value"}]},{"id":"blk-20276","spans":[{"id":"spn-21349","text":"Meaning"}]}],"id":"blk-20274","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20277","spans":[{"id":"spn-21350","marks":["code"],"text":"covariant"}]},{"id":"blk-20278","spans":[{"id":"spn-21351","text":"Subtype payloads acceptable on the consumer side"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20279","spans":[{"id":"spn-21352","marks":["code"],"text":"contravariant"}]},{"id":"blk-20280","spans":[{"id":"spn-21353","text":"Supertype payloads acceptable on the producer side"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20281","spans":[{"id":"spn-21354","marks":["code"],"text":"invariant"}]},{"id":"blk-20282","spans":[{"id":"spn-21355","text":"Exact payload schema match required"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20283","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21356","marks":["bold"],"text":"Required payload schemas:"},{"id":"spn-21357","text":" Each token gets its own JSON Schema under "},{"id":"spn-21358","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas/tokens/"},{"id":"spn-21359","text":". "},{"id":"spn-21360","marks":["bold"],"text":"Eight"},{"id":"spn-21361","text":" new schema files (the six v0.1.1 canonical tokens + two added in v0.2: "},{"id":"spn-21362","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationRequest"},{"id":"spn-21363","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21364","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionFidelityViolation"},{"id":"spn-21365","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-20284","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21366","text":"Token evolution rules (registry-level subtyping only)"}]},{"id":"blk-20285","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21367","text":"Token payload evolution happens "},{"id":"spn-21368","marks":["bold"],"text":"in the global registry, never per-loop"},{"id":"spn-21369","text":". This flows from OS-010 §1019–1051 (\"canonical tokens stable through v1.0; additive-only without minor bump; vendor-namespacing for custom tokens\")."}]},{"id":"blk-20286","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21370","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-21371","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive-only within a minor version."},{"id":"spn-21372","text":" Adding optional fields to a token's payload schema is allowed without bumping the token's version. Removing or renaming fields requires a minor version bump and 12-month notice (per OS-010 stability policy). 2. "},{"id":"spn-21373","marks":["bold"],"text":"Registry tracks the partial order."},{"id":"spn-21374","text":" The registry asserts "},{"id":"spn-21375","marks":["code"],"text":"topology_context.v0.2 <: topology_context.v0.1"},{"id":"spn-21376","text":" when the v0.2 schema is an additive extension of v0.1. The behavioral subtyping checker (§5) consults the registry rather than re-deriving compatibility. 3. "},{"id":"spn-21377","marks":["bold"],"text":"No per-loop token variants."},{"id":"spn-21378","text":" A loop that needs a custom payload must register a vendor-namespaced token (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-21379","marks":["code"],"text":"acme.v1.AcmeOutcome"},{"id":"spn-21380","text":") in the registry and reference it canonically from its manifest. Loops never declare local subtypes of canonical tokens — that would explode the cross-loop vocabulary and break PRISM's ability to benchmark heterogeneous systems against a shared evaluation grammar."}]},{"id":"blk-20287","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21381","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-20288","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21382","text":"2. Phase signatures with effect rows"}]},{"id":"blk-20289","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21383","marks":["bold"],"text":"Change:"},{"id":"spn-21384","text":" Extend the existing "},{"id":"spn-21385","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[]"},{"id":"spn-21386","text":" entries in "},{"id":"spn-21387","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.2.json"},{"id":"spn-21388","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-21389","marks":["code"],"text":"inputs"},{"id":"spn-21390","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21391","marks":["code"],"text":"outputs"},{"id":"spn-21392","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21393","marks":["code"],"text":"effects"},{"id":"spn-21394","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21395","marks":["code"],"text":"successors"},{"id":"spn-21396","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-21397","marks":["code"],"text":"refinements"},{"id":"spn-21398","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-20290","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"retrieve_context\",\n      \"kind\": \"retrieve\",\n      \"inputs\":  { \"tokens\": [], \"substrates\": [\"memory\"] },\n      \"outputs\": { \"tokens\": [\"TopologyContext\"] },\n      \"effects\": {\n        \"calls\":    [\"memory.retrieve_context\", \"memory.topology_analyze\"],\n        \"mutates\":  [],\n        \"may_emit\": [],\n        \"external\": []\n      },\n      \"successors\": [\"route_topology\"],\n      \"refinements\": {\n        \"latency_ms_max\": 200,\n        \"deterministic\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"route_topology\",\n      \"kind\": \"route\",\n      \"inputs\":  { \"tokens\": [\"TopologyContext\"], \"substrates\": [] },\n      \"outputs\": { \"tokens\": [] },\n      \"effects\": {\n        \"calls\":    [],\n        \"mutates\":  [],\n        \"may_emit\": [\"DeliberationRequest\"],\n        \"external\": []\n      },\n      \"successors\": [\"deliberate\", \"act_node_write\"],\n      \"refinements\": {\n        \"branch_predicate\": \"topology.routing\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-20291","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21399","marks":["bold"],"text":"Effect row fields:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20293","spans":[{"id":"spn-21400","text":"Field"}]},{"id":"blk-20294","spans":[{"id":"spn-21401","text":"What it tracks"}]}],"id":"blk-20292","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20295","spans":[{"id":"spn-21402","marks":["code"],"text":"calls"}]},{"id":"blk-20296","spans":[{"id":"spn-21403","text":"Substrate operation IDs invoked (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-21404","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-21405","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21406","marks":["code"],"text":"policy.check_policy"},{"id":"spn-21407","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20297","spans":[{"id":"spn-21408","marks":["code"],"text":"mutates"}]},{"id":"blk-20298","spans":[{"id":"spn-21409","text":"Substrate operation IDs that change state (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-21410","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.store_node"},{"id":"spn-21411","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21412","marks":["code"],"text":"audit.append_event"},{"id":"spn-21413","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20299","spans":[{"id":"spn-21414","marks":["code"],"text":"may_emit"}]},{"id":"blk-20300","spans":[{"id":"spn-21415","text":"Token names this phase may produce"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20301","spans":[{"id":"spn-21416","marks":["code"],"text":"external"}]},{"id":"blk-20302","spans":[{"id":"spn-21417","text":"External resources touched (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-21418","marks":["code"],"text":"http://*"},{"id":"spn-21419","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21420","marks":["code"],"text":"mcp://prism"},{"id":"spn-21421","text":")"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20303","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21422","marks":["bold"],"text":"Granularity is operation-level, not storage-level."},{"id":"spn-21423","text":" Effect rows reference the substrate API surface defined in OS-010 §9 (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-21424","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-21425","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21426","marks":["code"],"text":"audit.append_event"},{"id":"spn-21427","text":"), never specific storage paths like "},{"id":"spn-21428","marks":["code"],"text":"sqlite.kg.nodes"},{"id":"spn-21429","text":". This flows from the \"substrate independence\" thesis: the spec must not assume a relational backend, and graphonomous swapping SQLite for Postgres should not require manifest changes."}]},{"id":"blk-20304","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21430","marks":["bold"],"text":"Refinement values:"},{"id":"spn-21431","text":" key-value predicates. A small vendored evaluator handles the supported subset; unknown keys are passed through as documentation."}]},{"id":"blk-20305","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21432","marks":["bold"],"text":"Supported refinement predicates (vendored mini-evaluator):"}]},{"id":"blk-20306","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21433","text":"Comparison: "},{"id":"spn-21434","marks":["code"],"text":"≤"},{"id":"spn-21435","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21436","marks":["code"],"text":"<"},{"id":"spn-21437","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21438","marks":["code"],"text":"≥"},{"id":"spn-21439","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21440","marks":["code"],"text":">"},{"id":"spn-21441","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21442","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-21443","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21444","marks":["code"],"text":"!="},{"id":"spn-21445","text":" on numeric or string literals"}]}],"id":"blk-20307","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20310","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21446","text":"Boolean conjunction ("},{"id":"spn-21447","marks":["code"],"text":"∧"},{"id":"spn-21448","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-21449","marks":["code"],"text":"&&"},{"id":"spn-21450","text":") and disjunction ("},{"id":"spn-21451","marks":["code"],"text":"∨"},{"id":"spn-21452","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-21453","marks":["code"],"text":"||"},{"id":"spn-21454","text":") over the above"}]}],"id":"blk-20309","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21455","text":"Set membership: "},{"id":"spn-21456","marks":["code"],"text":"value in [a, b, c]"}]}],"id":"blk-20311","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20314","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21457","text":"Negation of any of the above"}]}],"id":"blk-20313","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-20315","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21458","text":"No Z3, no external SMT solver, no optional peer dependency. The vendored evaluator is a few hundred lines of TypeScript in "},{"id":"spn-21459","marks":["code"],"text":"src/refinement.ts"},{"id":"spn-21460","text":" and runs in any environment that runs npm. The ≤25KB processor target from STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW.md applies here too."}]},{"id":"blk-20316","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21461","text":"Recognized refinement keys in v0.2:"}]},{"id":"blk-20317","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20319","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21462","marks":["code"],"text":"latency_ms_max"},{"id":"spn-21463","text":" (number) — checker emits a benchmark assertion"}]}],"id":"blk-20318","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20321","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21464","marks":["code"],"text":"deterministic"},{"id":"spn-21465","text":" (boolean) — flagged in conformance T-DET"}]}],"id":"blk-20320","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20323","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21466","marks":["code"],"text":"branch_predicate"},{"id":"spn-21467","text":" (string) — referenced expression must appear in a"}]}],"id":"blk-20322","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-20324","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21468","text":"consumed token's payload schema"}]},{"id":"blk-20325","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20327","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21469","marks":["code"],"text":"idempotent"},{"id":"spn-21470","text":" (boolean) — extends existing T03 phase-idempotency check"}]}],"id":"blk-20326","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-20329","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21471","marks":["code"],"text":"requires_kappa"},{"id":"spn-21472","text":" (string, e.g. "},{"id":"spn-21473","marks":["code"],"text":"\"== 0\""},{"id":"spn-21474","text":", "},{"id":"spn-21475","marks":["code"],"text":"\"> 0\""},{"id":"spn-21476","text":") — routing precondition"}]}],"id":"blk-20328","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-20330","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21477","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-20331","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21478","text":"3. Local session type (derived, validated)"}]},{"id":"blk-20332","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21479","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not stored in the manifest"},{"id":"spn-21480","text":" — derived by the checker from the phase graph. Expressed internally as a regular expression over phase IDs (or an equivalent finite automaton)."}]},{"id":"blk-20333","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21481","text":"For graphonomous.continual_learning the derived session type is:"}]},{"id":"blk-20334","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"loop = retrieve_context · route_topology\n     · ( deliberate · act_node_write\n       | act_node_write )\n     · learn_outcome\n     · ( consolidate )?"},{"id":"blk-20335","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21482","marks":["bold"],"text":"Checker proves:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20337","spans":[{"id":"spn-21483","text":"Property"}]},{"id":"blk-20338","spans":[{"id":"spn-21484","text":"How"}]}],"id":"blk-20336","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20339","spans":[{"id":"spn-21485","marks":["bold"],"text":"Reachability"}]},{"id":"blk-20340","spans":[{"id":"spn-21486","text":"Every declared phase is reachable from an entry phase"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20341","spans":[{"id":"spn-21487","marks":["bold"],"text":"Progress"}]},{"id":"blk-20342","spans":[{"id":"spn-21488","text":"From any reachable phase a successor exists, or the loop terminates explicitly"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20343","spans":[{"id":"spn-21489","marks":["bold"],"text":"No deadlock"}]},{"id":"blk-20344","spans":[{"id":"spn-21490","text":"The successor relation has no cycles that can't make progress"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20345","spans":[{"id":"spn-21491","marks":["bold"],"text":"Token discipline"}]},{"id":"blk-20346","spans":[{"id":"spn-21492","text":"Every linear token emit has exactly one matching consumer reachable downstream; every affine has at most one"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20347","spans":[{"id":"spn-21493","marks":["bold"],"text":"Effect monotonicity"}]},{"id":"blk-20348","spans":[{"id":"spn-21494","text":"A phase's declared effect row is a superset of its successors' assumed reads"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20349","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21495","text":"Output of "},{"id":"spn-21496","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse check <manifest>"},{"id":"spn-21497","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-20350","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"✓ session type derives: retrieve · route · (deliberate? · act) · learn · consolidate?\n✓ all 8 canonical token consumers resolved\n✓ all linear tokens have unique consumers\n✓ all 7 invariants hold under refinement (vendored evaluator)\n✓ progress: from any reachable phase, a successor exists\n✓ liveness: retrieve is reachable from all phases"},{"id":"blk-20351","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21498","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-20352","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21499","text":"4. Global choreography + projection"}]},{"id":"blk-20353","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21500","marks":["bold"],"text":"Schema:"},{"id":"spn-21501","text":" "},{"id":"spn-21502","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas/pulse-choreography.v0.2.json"},{"id":"spn-21503","text":" (new) "},{"id":"spn-21504","marks":["bold"],"text":"File pattern:"},{"id":"spn-21505","text":" "},{"id":"spn-21506","marks":["code"],"text":"manifests/<name>.choreography.json"}]},{"id":"blk-20354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21507","text":"Choreographies live "},{"id":"spn-21508","marks":["bold"],"text":"alongside loop manifests in `manifests/`"},{"id":"spn-21509","text":", not in a separate top-level directory. This flows from the \"Topology as Authority\" thesis: a choreography is a higher-arity topology declaration (3+ participants) but still the same kind of artifact. Co-location keeps the authority for cross-loop topology in one place. No new "},{"id":"spn-21510","marks":["code"],"text":"choreographies/"},{"id":"spn-21511","text":" directory is created."}]},{"id":"blk-20355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21512","text":"Currently each manifest is local. v0.2 adds an optional "},{"id":"spn-21513","marks":["bold"],"text":"global type"},{"id":"spn-21514","text":" that describes the cross-loop dance and projects to per-loop connection blocks."}]},{"id":"blk-20356","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://opensentience.org/schemas/pulse-choreography.v0.2.json\",\n  \"choreography_id\": \"ecosystem.continual_learning_with_prism\",\n  \"version\": \"0.2.0\",\n  \"participants\": [\n    \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n    \"prism.benchmark\",\n    \"agentromatic.deliberation\"\n  ],\n  \"global_type\": [\n    {\n      \"step\": 1,\n      \"from\": \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n      \"to\":   \"agentromatic.deliberation\",\n      \"token\": \"DeliberationRequest\",\n      \"guard\": \"topology.kappa > 0\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 2,\n      \"from\": \"agentromatic.deliberation\",\n      \"to\":   \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n      \"token\": \"DeliberationResult\",\n      \"after\": [1]\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": 3,\n      \"from\": \"graphonomous.continual_learning\",\n      \"to\":   \"prism.benchmark\",\n      \"token\": \"OutcomeSignal\",\n      \"cadence\": \"per_action\",\n      \"after\":  [2]\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-20357","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21515","marks":["bold"],"text":"Projection algorithm."},{"id":"spn-21516","text":" Given a choreography C and participant P, produce the local view C↓P — a sequence of \"emit X\" / \"expect X\" obligations that the participant's PULSE manifest must satisfy. The checker then verifies each participant's "},{"id":"spn-21517","marks":["code"],"text":"connections"},{"id":"spn-21518","text":" block is consistent with its projection."}]},{"id":"blk-20358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21519","marks":["bold"],"text":"Soundness theorem (informal, follows MPST canon):"},{"id":"spn-21520","text":" If every participant locally type-checks against its projection, the choreography is *deadlock-free, communication-safe, and progresses to termination*."}]},{"id":"blk-20359","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21521","text":"A choreography can declare nesting (sub-choreographies) and parallel branches ("},{"id":"spn-21522","marks":["code"],"text":"parallel: [step_a, step_b]"},{"id":"spn-21523","text":") using existing PULSE primitives."}]},{"id":"blk-20360","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21524","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-20361","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21525","text":"5. Behavioral subtyping for version compatibility"}]},{"id":"blk-20362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21526","marks":["bold"],"text":"New CLI:"},{"id":"spn-21527","text":" "},{"id":"spn-21528","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse compat <loop_a@v> <loop_b@v>"}]},{"id":"blk-20363","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21529","text":"Replaces the de-facto policy of \"bump the version and pray\" with a machine-checked subtyping relation:"}]},{"id":"blk-20364","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"A <: B iff\n  phases:        A.phases ⊇ B.phases                       (extension allowed)\n  inputs:        ∀ p ∈ B: p_A.inputs    ⊆ p_B.inputs        (contravariant)\n  outputs:       ∀ p ∈ B: p_A.outputs   ⊇ p_B.outputs       (covariant)\n  effects:       ∀ p ∈ B: p_A.effects   ⊆ p_B.effects       (subeffecting)\n  linearity:     A.linear_tokens ⊇ B.linear_tokens          (no relaxation)\n  invariants:    A.invariants ⊇ B.invariants                (only added, not dropped)\n  cadence:       A.cadence refines B.cadence                (tighter, not looser)"},{"id":"blk-20365","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21530","text":"Output:"}]},{"id":"blk-20366","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ pulse compat graphonomous.continual_learning@0.4.3 \\\n              graphonomous.continual_learning@0.4.4\n\n✓ phases: superset (added: episodic_replay)\n✓ inputs: contravariant (no widenings broken)\n✓ outputs: covariant\n✓ effects: subeffecting holds\n✓ linearity: SurpriseSignal added as linear (additive)\n✓ invariants: superset (added: I7-episodic-monotonic)\n✓ cadence: unchanged\n\nVERDICT: 0.4.4 IS a safe behavioral subtype of 0.4.3."},{"id":"blk-20367","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21531","text":"Failed-compat verdict includes a counterexample trace."}]},{"id":"blk-20368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21532","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-20369","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21533","text":"6. Conformance checker (offline + runtime)"}]},{"id":"blk-20370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21534","marks":["bold"],"text":"Existing:"},{"id":"spn-21535","text":" "},{"id":"spn-21536","marks":["code"],"text":"src/conformance.ts"},{"id":"spn-21537","text":" already runs the 12 v0.1 tests. v0.2 adds:"}]},{"id":"blk-20371","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21538","marks":["bold"],"text":"Offline checks (new):"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20373","spans":[{"id":"spn-21539","text":"ID"}]},{"id":"blk-20374","spans":[{"id":"spn-21540","text":"Test"}]}],"id":"blk-20372","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20375","spans":[{"id":"spn-21541","text":"T13"}]},{"id":"blk-20376","spans":[{"id":"spn-21542","text":"Session-type derivation succeeds"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20377","spans":[{"id":"spn-21543","text":"T14"}]},{"id":"blk-20378","spans":[{"id":"spn-21544","text":"Reachability of all declared phases"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20379","spans":[{"id":"spn-21545","text":"T15"}]},{"id":"blk-20380","spans":[{"id":"spn-21546","text":"Progress (no stuck states)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20381","spans":[{"id":"spn-21547","text":"T16"}]},{"id":"blk-20382","spans":[{"id":"spn-21548","text":"Linear-token consumer uniqueness"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20383","spans":[{"id":"spn-21549","text":"T17"}]},{"id":"blk-20384","spans":[{"id":"spn-21550","text":"Affine-token consumer cap"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20385","spans":[{"id":"spn-21551","text":"T18"}]},{"id":"blk-20386","spans":[{"id":"spn-21552","text":"Effect row monotonicity"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20387","spans":[{"id":"spn-21553","text":"T19"}]},{"id":"blk-20388","spans":[{"id":"spn-21554","text":"Refinement satisfiability (vendored mini-evaluator)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20389","spans":[{"id":"spn-21555","text":"T20"}]},{"id":"blk-20390","spans":[{"id":"spn-21556","text":"Choreography projection consistency (if member)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21557","marks":["bold"],"text":"Runtime checks (new):"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20393","spans":[{"id":"spn-21558","text":"ID"}]},{"id":"blk-20394","spans":[{"id":"spn-21559","text":"Test"}]}],"id":"blk-20392","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20395","spans":[{"id":"spn-21560","text":"T21"}]},{"id":"blk-20396","spans":[{"id":"spn-21561","text":"Session fidelity — observed phase trace matches derived session type"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20397","spans":[{"id":"spn-21562","text":"T22"}]},{"id":"blk-20398","spans":[{"id":"spn-21563","text":"Linear-token actually-consumed-once (over trace window)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20399","spans":[{"id":"spn-21564","text":"T23"}]},{"id":"blk-20400","spans":[{"id":"spn-21565","text":"Effect-row honesty — observed substrate calls ⊆ declared "},{"id":"spn-21566","marks":["code"],"text":"calls"},{"id":"spn-21567","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-21568","marks":["code"],"text":"mutates"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21569","text":"On violation the checker emits a new canonical token, "},{"id":"spn-21570","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionFidelityViolation"},{"id":"spn-21571","text":", itself PULSE-typed, so violations flow through the same envelope plumbing as other signals."}]},{"id":"blk-20402","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21572","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-20403","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21573","text":"Token canon update"}]},{"id":"blk-20404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21574","text":"v0.2 adds two tokens to the canonical set:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20406","spans":[{"id":"spn-21575","text":"Token"}]},{"id":"blk-20407","spans":[{"id":"spn-21576","text":"Phase emitter"}]},{"id":"blk-20408","spans":[{"id":"spn-21577","text":"Linearity"}]},{"id":"blk-20409","spans":[{"id":"spn-21578","text":"Purpose"}]}],"id":"blk-20405","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20410","spans":[{"id":"spn-21579","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationRequest"}]},{"id":"blk-20411","spans":[{"id":"spn-21580","marks":["code"],"text":"route"}]},{"id":"blk-20412","spans":[{"id":"spn-21581","text":"linear"}]},{"id":"blk-20413","spans":[{"id":"spn-21582","text":"Triggers an inner deliberation loop (split out of overloaded routing)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20414","spans":[{"id":"spn-21583","marks":["code"],"text":"SessionFidelityViolation"}]},{"id":"blk-20415","spans":[{"id":"spn-21584","text":"conformance runtime"}]},{"id":"blk-20416","spans":[{"id":"spn-21585","text":"linear"}]},{"id":"blk-20417","spans":[{"id":"spn-21586","text":"Reports a runtime-observed protocol violation"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20418","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21587","text":"Total canonical tokens in v0.2: "},{"id":"spn-21588","marks":["bold"],"text":"8"},{"id":"spn-21589","text":" (was 6 in v0.1.1)."}]},{"id":"blk-20419","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21590","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-20420","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21591","text":"Backwards compatibility"}]},{"id":"blk-20421","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21592","text":"v0.1.1 manifests "},{"id":"spn-21593","marks":["bold"],"text":"continue to validate"},{"id":"spn-21594","text":" under v0.2 — every new field is optional. A v0.1.1 manifest validated under v0.2 schema receives:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-20423","spans":[{"id":"spn-21595","text":"Field"}]},{"id":"blk-20424","spans":[{"id":"spn-21596","text":"Default when absent"}]}],"id":"blk-20422","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-20425","spans":[{"id":"spn-21597","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].inputs"}]},{"id":"blk-20426","spans":[{"id":"spn-21598","marks":["code"],"text":"{ \"tokens\": [], \"substrates\": [] }"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20427","spans":[{"id":"spn-21599","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].outputs"}]},{"id":"blk-20428","spans":[{"id":"spn-21600","marks":["code"],"text":"{ \"tokens\": [] }"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20429","spans":[{"id":"spn-21601","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].effects"}]},{"id":"blk-20430","spans":[{"id":"spn-21602","marks":["code"],"text":"{ \"calls\": [], \"mutates\": [], \"may_emit\": [], \"external\": [] }"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20431","spans":[{"id":"spn-21603","marks":["code"],"text":"phases[].refinements"}]},{"id":"blk-20432","spans":[{"id":"spn-21604","marks":["code"],"text":"{}"}]}],[{"id":"blk-20433","spans":[{"id":"spn-21605","text":"Token registry lookups"}]},{"id":"blk-20434","spans":[{"id":"spn-21606","text":"Falls back to v0.1.1 implicit semantics (linear by default for canonical tokens, invariant, TTL = ∞)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-20435","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21607","text":"The checker reports v0.1.1-default manifests with "},{"id":"spn-21608","marks":["code"],"text":"degraded_checks: true"},{"id":"spn-21609","text":" — they pass T01–T12 but cannot pass T13–T23. Owners are nudged to enrich."}]},{"id":"blk-20436","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21610","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-20437","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21611","text":"Non-goals"}]},{"id":"blk-20438","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21612","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-21613","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not"},{"id":"spn-21614","text":" a process-algebra spec. PULSE v0.2 is session-typed, not CCS/CSP-modeled. Process-algebra-grade deadlock-freedom across parallel sub-agents is a future v0.3 question. 2. "},{"id":"spn-21615","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not"},{"id":"spn-21616","text":" an SMT/Z3 dependency. The refinement checker is a vendored mini-evaluator over ≤/≥/==/membership/conjunction/disjunction. Z3 is neither a runtime dependency nor an optional peer dep. If a complex constraint can't be evaluated locally, the checker emits a warning and runtime fidelity (T21–T23) catches violations. 3. "},{"id":"spn-21617","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not"},{"id":"spn-21618","text":" an MPST formalization paper. v0.2 follows MPST principles but targets working software, not formal verification literature."}]},{"id":"blk-20439","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21619","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-20440","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21620","text":"Resolved design questions (closed 2026-05-27)"}]},{"id":"blk-20441","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21621","text":"All five open questions are resolved against the project's stated thesis (see "},{"id":"spn-21622","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/V0.2-RATIONALE.md"},{"id":"spn-21623","text":" for the per-question evidence trail across OS-010, STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW.md, STACK_PLANNING.md, and the prompt set)."}]},{"id":"blk-20442","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21624","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-21625","marks":["bold"],"text":"Linearity default."},{"id":"spn-21626","text":" "},{"id":"spn-21627","marks":["bold"],"text":"Resolved: `linear`"},{"id":"spn-21628","text":" for new canonical tokens. Authors opt down to "},{"id":"spn-21629","marks":["code"],"text":"affine"},{"id":"spn-21630","text":" only for observational/idempotent/lossy- tolerant tokens. Flows from OS-010 §7.3 + §10.2 (\"fail loud, leave a trace; silent loss is an audit failure\"). 2. "},{"id":"spn-21631","marks":["bold"],"text":"Choreography artifact location."},{"id":"spn-21632","text":" "},{"id":"spn-21633","marks":["bold"],"text":"Resolved: co-located in `manifests/`."},{"id":"spn-21634","text":" No new top-level directory. Flows from STACK_TOPOLOGY_AS_AUTHORITY thesis — a choreography is a higher-arity topology artifact, same kind as a loop manifest. 3. "},{"id":"spn-21635","marks":["bold"],"text":"Effect row granularity."},{"id":"spn-21636","text":" "},{"id":"spn-21637","marks":["bold"],"text":"Resolved: operation-level, not storage-level."},{"id":"spn-21638","text":" Effect rows reference substrate API operations from OS-010 §9 (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-21639","marks":["code"],"text":"memory.retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-21640","text":"), never storage paths. Flows from \"substrate independence\" (OS-010 §3.4) and the \"falsifiable processor\" gate (STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW Finding 1). 4. "},{"id":"spn-21641","marks":["bold"],"text":"Refinement checker dependency."},{"id":"spn-21642","text":" "},{"id":"spn-21643","marks":["bold"],"text":"Resolved: vendor a tiny evaluator."},{"id":"spn-21644","text":" No Z3, no SMT, no optional peer dep. Covers ≤/≥/==/ membership/∧/∨/¬. Flows from \"tiny core, max portability\" and the ≤25KB processor target (STACK_ARCHITECTURE_GAP_REVIEW Finding 2). 5. "},{"id":"spn-21645","marks":["bold"],"text":"Per-loop token subtyping."},{"id":"spn-21646","text":" "},{"id":"spn-21647","marks":["bold"],"text":"Resolved: prohibited."},{"id":"spn-21648","text":" Token payload evolution happens only in the global registry, by additive-only rules. Custom payloads must vendor-namespace (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-21649","marks":["code"],"text":"acme.v1.X"},{"id":"spn-21650","text":"). Flows from OS-010 §1019–1051 (ecosystem-wide vocabulary stability) and STACK_PLANNING.md vendor-namespace pattern."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera66y6kczjnvjuiznjv5ekpnywr2msh6kgs2jxujqige46mmp7kfsq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}